{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015JC4ydwmbvBD9CqV333DbN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd059-version\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/version: Version Identity Binary\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  The project tags documentation releases (v0.YYYYMMDD.N) and code releases\n6\t  (v1.YYYYMMDD.N), but no binary reports which version it was built from.\n7\t  A cmd/version binary that prints the last known version tag gives a concrete,\n8\t  testable artifact that exercises the build pipeline before any utility code\n9\t  exists. It also provides a version string that other cmd/ binaries can import\n10\t  when they need to report their own version.\n11\t\n12\tgoals:\n13\t  - G1: Specify a cmd/version binary that prints the repository's last known version tag.\n14\t  - G2: Provide a version variable that other cmd/ packages can import.\n15\t\n16\trequirements:\n17\t  R1:\n18\t    title: cmd/version binary\n19\t    items:\n20\t      - R1.1:\n21\t          text: |\n22\t            Must provide a cmd/version/ package that compiles to a standalone binary. When\n23\t            invoked with no arguments, the binary prints the version string to stdout followed\n24\t            by a newline and exits 0.\n25\t      - R1.2:\n26\t          text: |\n27\t            The version string must be set at build time via -ldflags \"-X main.version=<tag>\".\n28\t            When the linker variable is not set (development builds), the binary must print\n29\t            \"dev\" as the version string.\n30\t      - R1.3:\n31\t          text: |\n32\t            The mage build target must resolve the version tag by running\n33\t            git describe --tags --abbrev=0 --match \"v[0-9]*\" and passing the result to the\n34\t            linker. If the git command fails (no tags, not a git repository), the build must\n35\t            succeed with the version set to \"dev\".\n36\t      - R1.4:\n37\t          text: |\n38\t            When invoked with --version or -v, the binary must print the same version string\n39\t            as the no-argument invocation. Any other flag must cause the binary to print a\n40\t            usage message to stderr and exit 2.\n41\t      - R1.5:\n42\t          text: |\n43\t            The version package must export a variable or function so that other cmd/ packages\n44\t            can import and report the same version string without duplicating the ldflags\n45\t            mechanism.\n46\t\n47\tnon_goals:\n48\t  - cmd/version does not parse LS_COLORS, handle signals, or do anything beyond printing a version string.\n49\t  - Build, lint, clean, and install mage targets are provided by cobbler-scaffold and not specified here.\n50\t\n51\tacceptance_criteria:\n52\t  - id: AC1\n53\t    criterion: \"mage build compiles cmd/version/ to bin/version. Running bin/version prints a version tag string (matching v[0-9]*) followed by a newline and exits 0.\"\n54\t    traces: [R1.1, R1.3]\n55\t  - id: AC2\n56\t    criterion: \"bin/version --version prints the same output as bin/version with no arguments.\"\n57\t    traces: [R1.4]\n58\t  - id: AC3\n59\t    criterion: \"bin/version --bogus prints a usage message to stderr and exits 2.\"\n60\t    traces: [R1.4]\n61\t  - id: AC4\n62\t    criterion: \"A development build (without ldflags) produces a binary that prints \\\"dev\\\".\"\n63\t    traces: [R1.2]\n64\t  - id: AC5\n65\t    criterion: \"The version package exports a variable or function importable by other cmd/ packages.\"\n66\t    traces: [R1.5]\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3973621-b5f4-4c44-adc3-0118bf6028ed","uuid":"a1749605-4d3b-46ae-870f-889ba39d591c","timestamp":"2026-05-14T00:46:35.368Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5109/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd059-version.yaml","content":"id: srd059-version\ntitle: \"cmd/version: Version Identity Binary\"\n\nproblem: |\n  The project tags documentation releases (v0.YYYYMMDD.N) and code releases\n  (v1.YYYYMMDD.N), but no binary reports which version it was built from.\n  A cmd/version binary that prints the last known version tag gives a concrete,\n  testable artifact that exercises the build pipeline before any utility code\n  exists. It also provides a version string that other cmd/ binaries can import\n  when they need to report their own version.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Specify a cmd/version binary that prints the repository's last known version tag.\n  - G2: Provide a version variable that other cmd/ packages can import.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: cmd/version binary\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: |\n            Must provide a cmd/version/ package that compiles to a standalone binary. When\n            invoked with no arguments, the binary prints the version string to stdout followed\n            by a newline and exits 0.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: |\n            The version string must be set at build time via -ldflags \"-X main.version=<tag>\".\n            When the linker variable is not set (development builds), the binary must print\n            \"dev\" as the version string.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: |\n            The mage build target must resolve the version tag by running\n            git describe --tags --abbrev=0 --match \"v[0-9]*\" and passing the result to the\n            linker. If the git command fails (no tags, not a git repository), the build must\n            succeed with the version set to \"dev\".\n      - R1.4:\n          text: |\n            When invoked with --version or -v, the binary must print the same version string\n            as the no-argument invocation. Any other flag must cause the binary to print a\n            usage message to stderr and exit 2.\n      - R1.5:\n          text: |\n            The version package must export a variable or function so that other cmd/ packages\n            can import and report the same version string without duplicating the ldflags\n            mechanism.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/version does not parse LS_COLORS, handle signals, or do anything beyond printing a version string.\n  - Build, lint, clean, and install mage targets are provided by cobbler-scaffold and not specified here.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"mage build compiles cmd/version/ to bin/version. Running bin/version prints a version tag string (matching v[0-9]*) followed by a newline and exits 0.\"\n    traces: [R1.1, R1.3]\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"bin/version --version prints the same output as bin/version with no arguments.\"\n    traces: [R1.4]\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"bin/version --bogus prints a usage message to stderr and exits 2.\"\n    traces: [R1.4]\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"A development build (without ldflags) produces a binary that prints \\\"dev\\\".\"\n    traces: [R1.2]\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"The version package exports a variable or function importable by other cmd/ packages.\"\n    traces: [R1.5]\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}}}
